<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00871</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>fda552ae-2fe7-4dcf-88fe-93552d4bb730</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="65237616-de74-4dfb-9289-08bbac93adec" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9a0e8228-dbbc-42d4-9bc8-0ea042e64963" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The bathtub starts out with no water." data-solution-options="[&quot;After 20 minutes, the bathtub is empty.&quot;, &quot;The bathtub starts out with no water.&quot;, &quot;After 10 minutes, the height of the water is 4 inches.&quot;, &quot;The height of the water is 10 inches after 4 minutes.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>1. The height of water in a bathtub, \(w\), is a function of time, \(t\). Let \(P\) represent this function. Height is measured in inches and time in minutes. </para>
      <para>What does each equation mean in this situation?</para>
      <para>\(P(0) = 0\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The bathtub starts out with no water.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3379ac21-fa25-4ce5-a6a6-1d8e84d30603" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The height of the water is 10 inches after 4 minutes." data-solution-options="[&quot;After 20 minutes, the bathtub is empty.&quot;, &quot;The bathtub starts out with no water.&quot;, &quot;After 10 minutes, the height of the water is 4 inches.&quot;, &quot;The height of the water is 10 inches after 4 minutes.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(P(4) = 10\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The height of the water is 10 inches after 4 minutes.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9026ab6b-c2b5-4f4c-b535-f7c79714eed2" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="After 10 minutes, the height of the water is 4 inches." data-solution-options="[&quot;After 20 minutes, the bathtub is empty.&quot;, &quot;The bathtub starts out with no water.&quot;, &quot;After 10 minutes, the height of the water is 4 inches.&quot;, &quot;The height of the water is 10 inches after 4 minutes.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(P(10) = 4\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! After 10 minutes, the height of the water is 4 inches.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e54beaa5-fe9d-410f-a372-7c182d63121a" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="After 20 minutes, the bathtub is empty." data-solution-options="[&quot;After 20 minutes, the bathtub is empty.&quot;, &quot;The bathtub starts out with no water.&quot;, &quot;After 10 minutes, the height of the water is 4 inches.&quot;, &quot;The height of the water is 10 inches after 4 minutes.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(P(20) = 0\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! After 20 minutes, the bathtub is empty.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9ba0c414-9e72-40cf-8171-f1a2008ab925" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(C(10:00)=English\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(C(English)=10:00\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(C(10:00)=English\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(C(Monday)=English\\) \\(at\\) \\(10:00\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(C(10:00)=Monday\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Function \(C\) takes time for its input and gives a student’s Monday class for its output.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(C(10:00)=English\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.2.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="db790a9a-4c23-4f64-99c6-d07ff5ce0469" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="3.1" data-solution-options="[&quot;3.0&quot;, &quot;3.1&quot;, &quot;3.2&quot;, &quot;3.3&quot;, &quot;3.4&quot;, &quot;3.5&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Function \(f\) gives the distance of a dog from a post, in feet, as a function of time, in seconds, since its owner left.</para>
      <figure><media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet.  "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/34491baf9eedf82892115acb6b6df9202640cb5e"/></media></figure><para> Find the value of \(f(20)\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(20)=3.1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="42a31a54-653c-4215-b686-a6f8274741d7" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="5" data-solution="3.5" data-solution-options="[&quot;3.0&quot;, &quot;3.1&quot;, &quot;3.2&quot;, &quot;3.3&quot;, &quot;3.4&quot;, &quot;3.5&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the value of \(f(140)\). </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(140)=3.5\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="908003dd-ec45-4360-990e-53b90e5315ba" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="In 1980, the world population increased by 83 million people." data-solution-options="[&quot;In 1980, the world population increased by 83 million people.&quot;, &quot;There were 83 million more people in 1980 than 1979.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Looking at the graph below, what does the point \((1980, 83)\) mean?</para>
      <figure><media alt="GRAPH TITLED &quot;WORLD POPULATION INCREASE&quot; WITH X-AXIS LABEL OF YEAR AND Y-AXIS LABEL OF MILLIONS OF PEOPLE"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/40b276fc71442a0f5c1ecb39fb8c84f44669ed72"/></media></figure></problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! In 1980, the world population increased by 80 million people.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.2.1 – 4.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0c5ed329-1ad3-4335-b6be-0b95861aeca4" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="After 6 hours, there was 5 inches of rain." data-solution-options="[&quot;At 6 hours, the rate is 5 inches per hour of rain.&quot;, &quot;After 5 hours, there was 6 inches of rain.&quot;, &quot;After 6 hours, there was 5 inches of rain.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Function \(R\) gives the number of inches of rain after \(h\) hours. What does the statement \(R(6)=5\) mean?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! After 6 hours, there was 5 inches of rain.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4d8f6467-07db-4c6e-9a41-a64633c2c719" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(T=R(h)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(R=T(h)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h=R(T)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h=T(R)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(T=R(h)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Function \(R\) gives the number of inches, \(T\), of rain after \(h\), hours. Choose which function notation represents this situation.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(T=R(h)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.2.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="821b6bf9-1c0c-45ce-9ef8-cfa4c4e4bd45" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(m=f(t)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f=m(t)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m=f(t)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t=m(f)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t=f(m)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use function notation to represent that the number of miles, \(m\), a car travels as a function of time, \(t\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! \(m=f(t)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.2.2 – 4.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
  </div>
</div></section>
